ratorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(-2,-3),$ $a=5$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e17fbd21a60b56f03ed40cebf7ae0d2f64b16f2af961e0289f78fb903d56fc" "basis" 1107 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3c3ab57d3f4eee40fa133cc881384f001d3a25c4d860095ddb8674be6cfd87" "basis" 1107 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e17fbd21a60b56f03ed40cebf7ae0d2f64b16f2af961e0289f78fb903d56fc" "basis" 1107 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=10\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/matha